{"date":"Tuesday 24 November 2026","updated":"16:00","sub":"Tuesday 24 November 2026 · GBP/USD · rebuilt in the evening after a publishing fault","tracker":"<div class=\"tk-row\">\n      <div class=\"tk s-off\" id=\"tkL\"><span class=\"light\"></span><div class=\"lab\"><span>London · BUY GBP/USD · no fill</span><em id=\"tkLs\"></em></div><div class=\"bar\"><i></i></div></div>\n      <div class=\"tk s-off\" id=\"tkN\"><span class=\"light\"></span><div class=\"lab\"><span>New York · not published</span><em id=\"tkNs\"></em></div><div class=\"bar\"><i></i></div></div>\n    </div>\n  ","feed":"<article class=\"post\" data-l=\"off\" data-lp=\"0\" data-n=\"off\" data-np=\"0\" data-t=\"06:40 UK\"><div class=\"time\">06:40<small>London brief</small></div><div class=\"body\"><span class=\"tag\" style=\"--k:var(--copper)\">London brief</span><h2>Buy the dip under the Asia low. Target: the Asia high.</h2><p class=\"lede\">The dollar was pushing into the bottom of a big monthly sell zone, and the pound sat just above its Asia low. The plan: let London dip under the Asia low, then buy the reclaim back into the range.</p><div class=\"plan\"><header><strong>GBP/USD</strong><span class=\"side buy\">BUY · CONTROL</span></header><dl><dt>Wait for</dt><dd>A dip under the Asia low 1.30324 (from 07:00)</dd><dt>Entry</dt><dd>1.30344 after the dip</dd><dt>Stop</dt><dd>1.30241 · about 10 pips</dd><dt>Target 1</dt><dd>1.30490 · about 15 pips</dd><dt>Target 2</dt><dd>1.30516 · Asia high</dd><dt>Status</dt><dd>Control: scored, not traded during the 07:00-10:00 test</dd></dl></div><p>This page was rebuilt in the evening: a publishing fault stopped the desk updating the website during the day. The calls below are the ones the desk made at the time.</p><section class=\"stage\" aria-label=\"Session chart\"><header><div><strong id=\"cPair\"></strong><small>15m · UK time</small></div><div class=\"views\" id=\"views\"></div></header>\n<svg class=\"chart\" id=\"chart\" viewBox=\"0 0 760 420\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Candlestick chart of the session with the desk's levels\"></svg><div class=\"pdk\" id=\"pdk\"></div><div class=\"scap\" id=\"cap\"></div></section></div></article>\n<article class=\"post\" data-l=\"off\" data-lp=\"0\" data-n=\"off\" data-np=\"0\" data-t=\"10:00 UK\"><div class=\"time\">10:00<small>London 10:00 call</small></div><div class=\"body\"><span class=\"tag\" style=\"--k:var(--gold)\">London 10:00 call</span><h2>Continuation: buy a pullback into the killzone equilibrium.</h2><p class=\"lede\">The killzone dipped under the Asia low at 07:05 (1.30295), then climbed 41 pips to 1.30707 by 09:55, taking the Asia high. With the leg finished and the dollar rejecting its monthly sell zone, the call was to buy a pullback to the middle of that leg.</p><div class=\"plan\"><header><strong>GBP/USD</strong><span class=\"side buy\">BUY · 10:00 CALL</span></header><dl><dt>Wait for</dt><dd>A pullback to the leg equilibrium, 10:00-11:30</dd><dt>Entry</dt><dd>1.30501</dd><dt>Stop</dt><dd>1.30405 · about 10 pips</dd><dt>Target</dt><dd>1.30707 · killzone high · about 21 pips</dd><dt>Cancel</dt><dd>Not filled by 11:30</dd></dl></div></div></article>\n<article class=\"post\" data-l=\"off\" data-lp=\"0\" data-n=\"off\" data-np=\"0\" data-t=\"12:00 UK\"><div class=\"time\">12:00<small>London review</small></div><div class=\"body\"><span class=\"tag\" style=\"--k:var(--green)\">London review</span><h2>No fill: the pullback never came.</h2><p class=\"lede\">Direction right, entry missed. Price only pulled back to 1.30608 at 10:35, 10.7 pips above the entry, then ran through last week's low to 1.30914 by noon. The 06:40 control would have filled at 07:00 and reached both targets by 08:35 (about +17 pips on paper, not counted during the test).</p><pre>SCORECARD  10:00 call · not triggered · 06:40 control · +17 pips on paper\nLondon high 1.30914 11:55 · low 1.30295 07:05</pre><p><b>What to learn:</b> on a trending morning the leg's equilibrium can be too deep. The second day running the direction was right and the pullback entry was missed.</p></div></article>\n<article class=\"post\" data-l=\"off\" data-lp=\"0\" data-n=\"off\" data-np=\"0\" data-t=\"16:00 UK\"><div class=\"time\">16:00<small>New York</small></div><div class=\"body\"><span class=\"tag\" style=\"--k:var(--blue)\">New York</span><h2>Not published today.</h2><p class=\"lede\">The New York brief and review were not published because of the same fault. GBP/USD kept rising through New York to 1.31179 by 14:55. Both desks publish normally again from Wednesday 06:40.</p></div></article>","week":"<section class=\"week\"><h3>Meridian 1 · week of 23 Nov · pips on the feed</h3><div class=\"wk\"><div class=\"\"><small>Mon</small><b class=\"\">—</b></div><div class=\"\"><small>Tue</small><b class=\"\">0 · no fill</b></div><div class=\"\"><small>Wed</small><b class=\"\">—</b></div><div class=\"\"><small>Thu</small><b class=\"\">—</b></div><div class=\"\"><small>Fri</small><b class=\"\">—</b></div><div class=\"tot\"><small>Week</small><b class=\"\">—</b></div></div></section>","chart":{"pair":"GBP/USD","bars":[["00:00",1.30332,1.30378,1.30332,1.30363],["00:15",1.30359,1.30368,1.30324,1.30342],["00:30",1.30342,1.30383,1.30332,1.30382],["00:45",1.30378,1.30433,1.30363,1.30404],["01:00",1.30408,1.30427,1.30387,1.30395],["01:15",1.30397,1.30475,1.30393,1.30466],["01:30",1.30468,1.3049,1.30455,1.30462],["01:45",1.30463,1.30478,1.30433,1.3045],["02:00",1.30442,1.30485,1.30439,1.30471],["02:15",1.30473,1.30485,1.30443,1.30455],["02:30",1.30459,1.30459,1.30414,1.30422],["02:45",1.3042,1.30439,1.30404,1.30409],["03:00",1.30412,1.30426,1.30367,1.30397],["03:15",1.30393,1.30414,1.3037,1.30381],["03:30",1.3038,1.30426,1.30371,1.30402],["03:45",1.30407,1.3042,1.304,1.30412],["04:00",1.30408,1.30429,1.30363,1.30387],["04:15",1.3038,1.304,1.30359,1.30373],["04:30",1.30378,1.30397,1.30356,1.30376],["04:45",1.30377,1.3048,1.30344,1.30406],["05:00",1.30405,1.30439,1.3039,1.3043],["05:15",1.30421,1